1. She previously worked at a zoo. (Verbatim: "so i worked at a zoo for for a while and i remember thinking these birds are on something they're heckin wild")

2. While working at the zoo, she had to handle high-energy animals like emus and ostriches. (Verbatim: "we had emus and ostriches though... they were just so high energy you just didn't know what they were gonna do")

3. She found animals like emus and ostriches intimidating due to their unpredictable energy. (Verbatim: "i don't want to mess with any big birds... especially emus and ostriches heck nah i'm never messing with any of those")

4. She believes orangutans are among the smartest animals, possibly smarter than some humans. (Verbatim: "orangutans are the smartest of them i think... they definitely be smarter than some people")

5. She is fascinated by animal intelligence and would like to do content about it. (Verbatim: "i really do want to do a zatsu about like different forms of intelligence because like animal like studying animal intelligence is such like an interesting topic for me")

6. She thinks octopuses are extremely difficult to contain and are very slippery creatures. (Verbatim: "octopi octopi i find would be they are they are truly the slipperiest slipperiest of creatures... really really really hard to contain")

7. She once had to walk a donkey that rolled on the floor, making the task difficult. (Verbatim: "the time i worked there... oh elia you just need to walk the donkey over there and i'm like okay and then the donkey's just rolling on the floor and i'm like i can't heckin do this")

8. She mentions a story from another zookeeper about an orangutan stealing a key and sneaking into the kitchen to drink squash. (Verbatim: "one of the keepers had accidentally dropped a key... it was getting through the door and drinking all the squash and then going back")

9. She believes bonobos are humans' closest ape relatives. (Verbatim: "i think the one that we're most genetically close to though is bonobos but yeah bonobos are our closest um ape relative i believe")

10. She has a personal tip for visiting zoos: wear the same color as zookeepers to get animals excited and engaged. (Verbatim: "if you're wearing the same color t-shirt or like same color like top as what their zoo keepers normally wear... the animals will be very excited to see you") [end of text]



1. She was responsible for looking after an axolotl in the past. (Verbatim: "i was responsible for the axolotl and they're so cute okay and so funny and they used to take up so much my time because like um basically i was responsible for having to feed the axolotl okay")

