10. She is aware of her relative obscurity compared to pandas and jokes about it self-deprecatingly. (Verbatim: "people know more about elias delaria than pandas i'm joking by the way... i am painfully aware pandas are more known than british vtuber elias delaria") [end of text]



1. She is mixed race and grew up with a mix of Asian and British cuisine. (Verbatim: "because i'm i'm mixed race i've always grown up with like a mix of asian and british cuisine")
2. Her father, Papa Elia, cooked traditional English dinners every Sunday. (Verbatim: "every sunday we'd have a traditional english dinner cooked by papa elia")
3. She grew up eating homemade slow-cooked British dishes like cottage pie, shepherd’s pie, and stew. (Verbatim: "they'd normally be slow cooked throughout the day... mostly cottage pie though and the cheese on top")
4. She dislikes stew and used to be sad when it was served as a child. (Verbatim: "i used to be so sad on the days we'd have stew i'd be like now i want college boy")
5. Her English grandmother (nan) enjoys cooking with a slow cooker and still cooks for herself despite her age. (Verbatim: "my nan on my english side cooks all of that sort of stuff as well like she adores her slow cooker")
6. She has a fondness for cute themed food, especially panda-shaped steamed buns and Japanese food. (Verbatim: "they have a little like stool for like panda shaped food it is so cute i'll never get over the cute food in japan")
7. She loves pastry, particularly meat pies like chicken and mushroom, steak and ale, and chicken and leek. (Verbatim: "we love brown yeah give me that pie... the other chicken pie is chicken and leek")
8. In England, "pie" typically refers to savory meat pies rather than fruit desserts. (Verbatim: "if someone offers you a pie in england they are not chatting about the fruit they are not chatting about dessert they're chatting about dinner")
9. She finds British cuisine uncolorful and generally brown, with limited use of spices beyond salt and pepper. (Verbatim: "all the foods I've mentioned are brown they're not very colorful... we don't seem to like color or a spice")
10. She finds pandas and links (likely meant as "lynx") cute and has seen bears in a zoo during a rare post-hibernation moment. (Verbatim: "the ultra rare bear moment was the moment the bear comes out of hibernation it was so cute... links are really cute though") [end of text]



1. She previously worked with animals in a zoo setting, including breeding programs. (Verbatim: "one of the things that's really common in zoos is like trying to get them to like mate... I had to look after lemurs and when I had to look after the lemurs...")

