5. She expresses fondness for animals that form close pairs or bonds. (Verbatim: "they'll follow them around everywhere... i'm coming with you i'm going alone you're not going alone mr frodo i'm coming with you.")

6. She had difficulty communicating due to a perceived "British debuff" and questioned her pronunciation. (Verbatim: "oh the british debuff is real i did say lemurs right like oh dear.")

7. She cared for a hand-reared vulture that could not fly and behaved like a human. (Verbatim: "this vulture... thinks it's a human... it doesn't know how to fly it just walks around on his little feet.")

8. She shows empathy toward rejected or isolated animals and tried to support them. (Verbatim: "i got your back lemur don't you worry i got you... i'm gonna give you all the food ain't nobody gonna bully you ever again.")

9. She finds the name "blue-footed booby" amusing and memorable. (Verbatim: "the blue-footed booby is always I will never get over the blue-footed boobies... boobies this is boobies it's boobies.")

10. She notes that animal bullying occurs across species and is a common issue in group dynamics. (Verbatim: "you bullying happens no matter the species... they'll always be that one that's like separate.") [end of text]



